      "In WEAK_CONDITIONAL_STRONG_MARGINAL, aligned direct-regret gain beat shuffled controls only 3/5 despite very high apparent capture, so direct value maximization can also become insufficiently alignment-specific under weak conditional structure.",
      "The candidate is not qualified for consumed TRAIN-only market shadow or canonical replacement."
    ],
    "cross_experiment_localization": "Across M2.2, M2.2B, M2.2C, M2.2D, and M2.2E, the tradeoff is now repeatedly falsified from different directions. Strong Champion anchoring suppresses harm but under-corrects; value-sensitive weighting and direct utility objectives improve correction but increase harmful movement; pairwise ordering is alignment-sensitive and safer than absolute CE but does not universally improve Champion-relative value. No tested Direction loss family simultaneously produces robust alignment dependence, advantage capture, net gain, and harm suppression across all four preregistered regimes.",
    "broader_implication": "The evidence no longer supports continuing to treat loss-shape selection as the primary bottleneck. The next work must move upstream to Teacher temporal transport/calibration and downstream to Student representation/generalization/gradient topology. The learning philosophy itself remains unrefuted because state-conditioned signal repeatedly exists, but it must now be tested at the mechanism level rather than by inventing another Direction objective."
